Description: log @tasks_install + @cmd to syslog for diagnostic
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-16
Bug-Athena: TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC PATCH (revert when bug is fixed).
 Operator reports tasksel's interactive dialog "checking the box has
 no effect" — selecting athena-development-tools or athena-gnome via
 the multiselect menu doesn't trigger an apt-get install for those
 tasks' Key packages.  Meanwhile, CLI-mode `tasksel install
 athena-gnome` DOES trigger apt-get install (and proceeds to install
 packages, until it hits a separate cascade of postinst failures
 around ca-certificates).
 .
 Code review of /usr/bin/tasksel and tasksel-debconf shows the
 interactive flow:
   1. interactive() builds @list from displayed tasks
   2. tasksel-debconf invokes db_input + db_get, writes selection to
      a tmpfile
   3. interactive() reads tmpfile, calls list_to_tasks($ret, @tasks)
      to map selection to task hashes, sets _install=1 on each
   4. main() builds @tasks_install = grep { _install } @tasks
   5. if @tasks_install non-empty, push task_packages onto @cmd and
      run apt-get install
 .
 Code review can't show what's actually happening at runtime —
 specifically, what @tasks_install contains right before the apt-get
 call.  This patch adds a single `print STDERR` line that logs the
 task names in @tasks_install to syslog (which lands in
 athena_efi.log thanks to pkgsel.postinst's `--logstderr` argument
 to debconf-apt-progress).
 .
 Expected diagnostic output in next install's syslog:
 .
   tasksel-debug: about to run apt-get install
   tasksel-debug: tasks_install=[athena-gnome,standard]
   tasksel-debug: tasks_remove=[]
   tasksel-debug: cmd-package-count=N
 .
 Where N is the actual number of packages tasksel is passing to
 apt-get install.  If N==0 or matches only the standard task's
 expansion (~12 packages on our pool), we've confirmed the user's
 dialog-checkbox selection didn't reach @tasks_install.  Next step
 then narrows further into interactive() / list_to_tasks /
 tasksel-debconf.
 .
 If N matches expected for the selected tasks, the bug is elsewhere
 (in apt-get itself or the wrapper).
 .
 REMOVE THIS PATCH ONCE THE ROOT-CAUSE IS IDENTIFIED.  It's a
 noise-adding patch that doesn't belong in steady-state.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/tasksel.pl
+++ b/tasksel.pl
@@ -923,6 +923,15 @@
 	push @cmd, qw{apt-get -q -y -o APT::Install-Recommends=true -o APT::Get::AutomaticRemove=true -o Acquire::Retries=3 install};

 	# And finally, act on selected tasks.
+	# Athena DIAGNOSTIC: log what we're about to install.  Revert when
+	# the dialog-checkbox-has-no-effect bug is fixed.
+	print STDERR "tasksel-debug: about to run apt-get install\n";
+	print STDERR "tasksel-debug: tasks_install=[" .
+	    join(",", map { $_->{task} } @tasks_install) . "]\n";
+	print STDERR "tasksel-debug: tasks_remove=[" .
+	    join(",", map { $_->{task} } @tasks_remove) . "]\n";
+	my $pkg_count = scalar(map { task_packages($_) } @tasks_install);
+	print STDERR "tasksel-debug: cmd-package-count=$pkg_count\n";
 	if (@tasks_install || @tasks_remove) {
 		foreach my $task (@tasks_remove) {
 			push @cmd, map { "$_-" } task_packages($task);
